# Analysis (epic «Бизнес-анализ», feature «Аналитика»)
File id only: this is `playbook-step-01-analysis.mdc`, not a column number.

Input: the issue and, for a feature, the parent epic page. Output: the analysis section on that page. Product WHY and WHAT only. Finish it before any architecture text.

No services, API paths, storage, migrations, or contracts in this section (those belong in Архитектура). Which blocks apply follows `playbook-workflow.mdc`.

The wiki section is text. Do not put a status line on the page. The stage is the issue label.

## Which blocks apply
- Epic column Бизнес-анализ: the epic blocks below. Outcome: enough to choose architecture and to split features. Not a screen specification. Does not unlock feature code.
- The standing bugs epic uses the same blocks. The text may be short. It still says why this class of work exists.
- Feature column Аналитика, including a bug-feature: the feature blocks below. Inherit the epic's chosen user story. Re-open the epic goal only when it changes.
- A typo, or a 500 caused by a typo, inside an open feature: no new page and no new issue. Fix that feature.
- A substantial product change (add or remove a field, change a screen, change a business rule) is a bug-feature and uses this section.

## Epic blocks (Бизнес-анализ)
1. Problem now. What hurts, what already works (name the `Doc-` pages), and what must not break.
2. Actors. Roles and when they care. Not tokens or JWT.
3. Named analogues. Name each comparable product or pattern, what it does, and why it fits or does not fit. "Like other sites" with no name is not evidence.
4. Several solution options on a continuum. More than one option, ordered along one axis (for example smaller change to larger change).
5. Chosen user story, and why it is the best fit for us.
6. Non-goals.

No field catalog. No services. No screen layout.

## Feature blocks (Аналитика)
1. Inherit the epic. Restate the epic goal only when this feature changes it.
2. Every proposed field, control, or block, on a screen or only in the backend: who fills or supplies it, who reads it, why it exists, lifecycle (create, edit, empty, error), and how it looks and behaves. A passport field the service accepts or stores is a product decision. Prefer omit: if the item does not earn its place, leave it out.
3. Layout, when a screen is proposed: grouping, primary action, and behavior. A pixel mock only when the behavior stays unclear without it.
4. Given/When/Then for the behavior this feature must show.
5. Open questions, if any. List them unanswered in «Решения» (`playbook-step-03-decisions.mdc`). Do not invent a column for them.

A bug-feature covers the product change (the field, the screen, or the rule). It does not add unrelated fields.

## Done when
- Epic: all six epic blocks are visible, analogues are named, there is more than one option on a continuum, the chosen user story says why it is best for us, and the page has no field catalog and no services.
- Feature: a developer cannot invent a field or block this section did not justify. Every proposed field or block has who fills it, who reads it, why, lifecycle, and look/behavior. A proposed screen has layout. Given/When/Then are present. A name-only field list is not done.
- Do not open Архитектура while this bar fails.
